{title: Joy to the World}
{artist: Isaac Watts & Lowell Mason}
{key: D}
{time: 2/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[D]Joy to the world! the [G]Lord is [D]come:
let earth re[A]ceive her [D]King;
let every [D]heart prepare him room,
and heaven and nature sing,
and [A]heaven and nature sing,
and [D]heaven, and [G]heaven and [D]nature sing.

Verse 2
[D]Joy to the earth, [G]the [D]Savior
reigns! Let men their [D]songs
employ; While [D]fields and floods, rocks,
hills and plains Repeat the
sounding [A]joy, Repeat the sounding
joy, [D]Repeat, repeat, [G]the [D]sounding joy.

Verse 3
[D]No more let sins and sorrows [G]grow, Nor thorns [D]infest
the ground; He comes [D]to
make His [D]blessings flow Far as
the curse is found, Far
as [A]the curse is found,
Far [D]as, far [G]as, the curse [D]is found.

Verse 4
[D]He rules the world [G]with [D]truth
and grace, And makes [D]the
nations prove [D]The glories of His
righteousness, And wonders of His
love, [A]And wonders of His
love, [D]And wonders, [G]wonders, of [D]His love.
